---
// The notice at the top of every CLI page. One copy, so the wording stays the same everywhere.
---

<aside class="starlight-aside starlight-aside--caution girt-cli-notice" aria-label="Not a Git replacement">
  <p class="starlight-aside__title">Not a Git replacement</p>
  <div class="starlight-aside__content">
    <p>
      The <code>girt</code> command exists to exercise the girt library: to show that each Git operation can be
      built on it, and to give a surface for byte-for-byte and performance comparisons with Git. It is not meant to
      replace <code>git</code>. Command names and options are girt's own and may change in any release; the
      library is the product.
    </p>
  </div>
</aside>
